# <src>                  <mnt_point>  <type>  <mnt_flags and options>  <fs_mgr_flags>   (fstab version 2, KitKat)
#
# NOTE: mmcblk0p3 is NOT a dedicated misc/BCB partition -- it is the MBR
# extended-partition container that holds p5/p6/p7/p8 as logical partitions
# (confirmed via MBR dump 2026-09-29: partition 3 entry type=0x05, spanning
# the full ~2GB that contains system/cache/device/factory). The stock
# recovery.fstab (extracted from the untouched OEM recovery.img) has no
# /misc entry at all -- this device's reboot-to-recovery persistence is a
# hardware (SNVS/watchdog scratch register) mechanism, not a misc-partition
# BCB. An earlier build of this fstab incorrectly mapped /misc here; TWRP's
# own BCB-clearing write on shutdown/reboot zeroed the first ~8MB of the
# extended partition (its EBR chain) as a result, taking system/cache with
# it until the EBR chain was manually reconstructed. Do not add /misc back
# without a verified, dedicated partition for it.
/dev/block/mmcblk0p1    /boot       emmc    defaults    defaults
/dev/block/mmcblk0p2    /recovery   emmc    defaults    defaults
/dev/block/mmcblk0p5    /system     ext4    defaults    defaults
/dev/block/mmcblk0p6    /cache      ext4    defaults    defaults
/dev/block/mmcblk0p4    /data       ext4    defaults    defaults
/dev/block/mmcblk0p7    /device     ext4    defaults    defaults
/dev/block/mmcblk0p8    /factory    ext4    defaults    defaults
